    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, that \"long-term growth\" thing feels pretty speculative and theoretical. if u look at it from a practical standpoint, the immediate destruction of the manufacturing base and the energy independence we have now is a much more certain outcome. isn't the most realistic economic take that the sheer scale of the transition would cause more harm than good before any \"green jobs\" actually materialize?",
